WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
The Analyze phase asks why the course should exist.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:08.339
Start with the business, operational, compliance, or performance problem.

3
00:00:08.339 --> 00:00:10.964
Is there a behavior that needs to change?

4
00:00:10.964 --> 00:00:13.667
A task that is performed inconsistently?

5
00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.906
A policy that learners must apply?

6
00:00:15.906 --> 00:00:18.068
A decision that causes mistakes?

7
00:00:18.068 --> 00:00:23.627
The clearer the problem, the easier it becomes to decide what the course should teach.

8
00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:25.634
Audience analysis is central.

9
00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:37.371
Identify who the learners are, what they already know, what they struggle with, what language or examples will make sense to them, and what constraints affect their participation.

10
00:00:37.371 --> 00:00:43.316
A course for new hires needs different pacing than a course for experienced practitioners.

11
00:00:43.316 --> 00:00:50.188
A course for field workers may need different delivery assumptions than a course for office-based staff.

12
00:00:50.188 --> 00:00:53.894
Task analysis separates information from performance.

13
00:00:53.894 --> 00:01:03.005
People may need information, but training is usually justified because people need to do, decide, recognize, avoid, or explain something.

14
00:01:03.005 --> 00:01:13.429
Breaking down the task helps identify required knowledge, common mistakes, decision points, tools used, and the conditions under which performance happens.

15
00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:17.212
This prevents the course from becoming a catalog of facts.

16
00:01:17.212 --> 00:01:32.191
Analysis also includes constraints: delivery environment, device expectations, seat time, accessibility needs, translation needs, regulatory requirements, LMS tracking, review timelines, and available source material.

17
00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:35.511
These constraints are not administrative trivia.

18
00:01:35.511 --> 00:01:40.762
They shape course length, media choices, navigation, assessment, and rollout.

19
00:01:40.762 --> 00:01:45.394
Finally, analysis should ask whether eLearning is the right solution.

20
00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:54.274
If the problem is lack of access, broken process design, unclear policy, missing tools, or poor incentives, a course alone may not fix it.

21
00:01:54.274 --> 00:02:06.859
ADDIE is strongest when it helps the team define the right intervention, even when that intervention includes job aids, manager support, process changes, or coaching in addition to eLearning.
